reply.body:
Ok, I think I understand your approach now. Please confirm if I understand correctly:

Follow the path until no more path elements can be looked up in the source map. At that point, emit a suffix map where the suffix is either:

- The key of the value to replace in the map that was traversed to
- The path elements that could not be looked up

If we traverse to a list of maps, fail because it is ambiguous which map we should modify.

Putting it all together, if we had this source map:

```json
{
  "path1": {
    "path2.path3": {
      "key1": "value1"
    }
  }
}
```

And we wanted to insert `"path1.path2.path3.key2": "value2"`, the result should be:

```json
{
  "path1": {
    "path2.path3": {
      "key1": "value1",
      "key2": "value2"
    }
  }
}
```

Do I understand correctly?

